literal-block: '''
	''''
	still content
	'''
escaped-block: """
	""""
	still content
	"""
literal-unicode: 'before middle after'
escaped-unicode: "before middle after"
empty-keys: [{'': 1}, {"": 2}]
/* x /*/
after-comment: true

----------------------------------------------------

[
	["key", "literal-block"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	["block-string", "'''\r\n\t''''\r\n\tstill content\r\n\t'''"],
	["key", "escaped-block"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	["block-string", "\"\"\"\r\n\t\"\"\"\"\r\n\tstill content\r\n\t\"\"\""],
	["key", "literal-unicode"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	["string", "'before\u2028middle\u2029after'"],
	["key", "escaped-unicode"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	["string", "\"before\u2028middle\u2029after\""],
	["key", "empty-keys"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	["punctuation", "["],
	["punctuation", "{"],
	["key", "''"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	["number", "1"],
	["punctuation", "}"],
	["punctuation", ","],
	["punctuation", "{"],
	["key", "\"\""],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	["number", "2"],
	["punctuation", "}"],
	["punctuation", "]"],
	["comment", "/* x /*/"],
	["key", "after-comment"],
	["punctuation", ":"],
	["boolean", "true"]
]

----------------------------------------------------

Longer quote runs remain block-string content in both quote styles. Literal U+2028 and U+2029 stay inside single-line strings. Empty quoted keys are properties. The slash before a block comment terminator belongs to its body, and tokenization resumes after the terminator.
